{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03R0", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0b4ad01ce2a0bac8c191f95e8004c8c8464fec043f9172a3fa00f7432c71b37", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe next task at hand is to compute the <ACCENT_0001>tale cohomology of a smooth curve\nover an algebraically closed field with torsion coefficients, and in\nparticular show that it vanishes in degree at least 3. To prove this, we\nwill compute cohomology at the generic point, which\namounts to some Galois cohomology.\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47efaa722623a3c2aec5b37815b43d1e1b464a991feaaf2feb5cf2b81102ac17", "unit_id": "tag:03R0:prose-0001"}
